# Raw Python Image Processing Engine

A high-performance, command-line image editing tool built from scratch in pure Python.
No OpenCV. No NumPy. Just raw matrix manipulations and heavily optimized algorithmic design. 

This project demonstrates a deep understanding of core computational photography algorithms and time/space complexity optimizations.

## Key Features & Algorithmic Optimizations
* **O(1) Adaptive Edge Detection:** Implements a Summed Area Table (Integral Image) algorithm,
dropping the time complexity of local-mean thresholding to exactly O(N) for the entire image, regardless of block size.
* **Lightning-Fast Pixel Mapping:** Uses pre-computed Look-Up Tables (LUTs) and C-optimized nested list comprehensions for O(1) quantization, grayscale conversion, and color manipulation.
* **Optimized Matrix Convolutions:** Implements "clamp-to-edge" image padding to entirely remove innermost bounds-checking during kernel matrix dot-products.

